29️⃣ What is event-driven programming?

It’s a programming paradigm where code runs in response to events (like user click, API response, or payment success).
Node.js uses an event-driven architecture — ideal for async tasks.

30️⃣ What is the difference between synchronous and asynchronous code in Node.js?

Synchronous code blocks execution until finished; asynchronous code runs in the background (using callbacks/promises).
This improves performance for I/O-heavy tasks like database calls.

